  "applies_to": "A Fronius Sensor Card connected to a Fronius Datamanager over Solar Net and republished by it as a SunSpec device; the same layout is used for the float and int+SF settings.",
  "summary": "The Datamanager publishes each Fronius Sensor Card as its own Modbus device (unit ID 245 for Solar Net address 0, up to 247). After the common block it carries SunSpec irradiance model 302, back-of-module temperature model 303 and base meteorological model 307. This map covers the identification block, irradiance, both temperature inputs and wind speed.",
  "transport": [
    "TCP",
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 245,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "Fronius numbers registers from 1 (SunSpec base register 40001) and tells you to request the register number minus one, so register 40072 is read at wire address 40071. The manual's RTU example reads register 40005 with address bytes 9C 44 (40004)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": "Register map archive version 1.1.7-0 (IG_Sensor_Card_Register_Map_Float_and_Int&SF_v1.0.xlsx); manual 42,0410,2049 rev. 033-24022026.",
  "source": {
    "title": "Fronius Datamanager Modbus TCP & RTU (operating instructions) + IG_Sensor_Card_Register_Map_Float_and_Int&SF_v1.0.xlsx",
    "doc_number": "42,0410,2049 (033-24022026)",
    "revision_date": "2026-02",
    "url": "https://www.fronius.com/en/~/downloads/Solar%20Energy/Operating%20Instructions/42,0410,2049.pdf",
    "pages": "PDF English part: printed p. 66 (Modbus device ID for Fronius Sensor Cards: offset 245); register table = XLSX 'Complete Map' sheet in https://www.fronius.com/en/~/downloads/Solar%20Energy/Operating%20Instructions/SE_EI_Modbus_Sunspec_Maps_State_Codes_Events_EN.zip"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Register table from Fronius' official XLSX in the Modbus SunSpec maps ZIP; the unit-ID rule comes from the PDF.",
    "The XLSX gives a fixed scale factor of -1 for the temperatures (raw x 0.1); GHI and wind speed have no scale factor and are used as read.",
    "Left out: the 32-bit SID (40001-40002, word order not stated) and every point the XLSX marks not supported (POAI, DFI, DNI, OTI, the second TmpBOM at 40080, RH, pressure, wind direction, rain, snow, precipitation type, electric field, surface and soil wetness).",
    "Changelog 1.1.5-0 notes that TmpAmb (40083) is mapped to temperature sensor 2 and the second TmpBOM register is not supported."
  ],
